#
# Conformance case: nominal-counting/oneof-differentfrom-clash
# AC (Family 4, native nominal-counting refutation): a pure nominal pigeonhole clash
# forces two distinct individuals into a ONE-element nominal set — an inconsistency
# the native forward chase cannot see (it carries no nominal-equality/counting
# reasoning) but the case-split / counting refutation sub-deciders
# (crates/logic/src/reason/refute/{casesplit,counting}.rs) decide soundly and
# completely.
#
# The world-scoped EDB (input.nq) types `x` to the singleton enumeration
# `owl:oneOf (a)` and `y` to the singleton enumeration `owl:oneOf (a)`, so both `x`
# and `y` are forced equal to the sole nominal `a` (x = a = y). But the EDB also
# asserts `x owl:differentFrom y`. Two pigeons (`x`, `y`), one hole (`a`): the forced
# equality contradicts the declared distinctness, so the world is INCONSISTENT. The
# refutation kernel materializes the nominal clash and the native token is a clean
# `inconsistent` (empty `gaps`) rather than `incomplete`.
#
# No committed W3C OWL 2 Full divergence slug is PURELY nominal (they entangle harder
# existential/cardinality constructs and stay withheld), so this endogenous fixture
# is Family 4's decided on-gate production demonstration — the datatest harness runs
# the real `gmeow_logic::reason::dl_consistency` over input.nq and grades the verdict.
#
# verdict_mode=consistency: the OWL EDB is the world-scoped N-Quads in input.nq,
# decided by the native DL path (gmeow_logic::reason::dl_consistency); this file
# exists only to satisfy the per-case anatomy and is NOT compiled in consistency mode.
#
# Graph-isolation note: this fixture lives in the conformance corpus, OUTSIDE the
# production owl:imports closure by construction — it can never make the production
# ontology appear inconsistent.
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
